From 2623c1b368b432f46959e3bfc9b0a6c73f63f416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:57:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): blocked decision cards on the hub skip
 the admission judge

A hub chat could not file a decision card at all (t_01a1cf9334ff49bc): kanban_create with
initial_status='blocked' + human_request was refused 4x with placement_unavailable. The blocked
status/human_request are courier-uncarried options, so structural_reason made the card an explicit
hub pin, the judge denied it ("no hub-only capability is required"), and the refusal then told the
caller to "use placement='local'" -- which is what it had passed.

- A hub-candidate card created blocked on a human_request (placement omitted/auto/local/here) is
  created with no judge call. Its work goes where a denied card goes (worker queue or worker-first,
  hub:write for hub-state wording), so after unblock it runs in the pool, never on a hub slot. The
  hub_admission event records skipped=blocked_decision_card. With no pool it is created here.
- Still judged: ready cards, an explicit hub pin, runs_on machine:hub / hub-only labels, force_hub,
  and decision cards with another structural keep-local (host workspace, other board).
- A hub-origin stay-here refusal names alternatives that work there (omit placement -> pool,
  hub_reason, or a blocked decision card) instead of placement='local'.
